      "completion_tokens": 1167,
      "output": "At its most basic level, **water** is a chemical compound. Its scientific name is **dihydrogen monoxide**, but it is most commonly known by its chemical formula: **$H_2O$**.\n\nHere is a breakdown of what that means and why water is unique:\n\n### 1. Chemical Structure\nWater is made up of two elements:\n*   **Hydrogen:** A gas that is extremely light and flammable.\n*   **Oxygen:** A gas that we need to breathe to survive.\n\nWater is formed when two hydrogen atoms bond with one oxygen atom. This bond is called a covalent bond, where the atoms share electrons.\n\n### 2. Key Properties\nWater is not just a random liquid; it has specific physical and chemical traits that make it essential for life:\n\n*   **Polarity:** The oxygen atom pulls electrons away from the hydrogen atoms, giving water a \"magnetic\" quality. One end of the molecule is slightly negative, and the other is slightly positive. This allows water molecules to stick to each other (cohesion) and to other substances (adhesion).\n*   **Universal Solvent:** Because of its polarity, water can dissolve more substances than any other liquid. This is why it is the main transport medium in the human body and in nature (carrying nutrients and waste).\n*   **States of Matter:** Water can exist in all three states:\n    *   **Solid (Ice):** When frozen, water molecules move slowly and form a rigid crystal lattice.\n    *   **Liquid:** The state we see every day.\n    *   **Gas (Steam):** When heated, water molecules move so fast they escape into the air.\n*   **Density Anomaly:** Unlike most substances, water is **less dense** as a solid (ice) than as a liquid. This is why ice floats on water. If ice sank, lakes and oceans would freeze solid from the bottom up, killing all aquatic life.\n\n### 3. Why It Is Important\nWater is the foundation of life on Earth. It acts as a chemical reactant in photosynthesis and respiration, regulates body temperature, lubricates joints, and cushions organs. Without water, life as we know it could not exist."
